WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.940
<b>Beta</b>

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:08.900
What?!

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:14.090
What's all this dwama about?

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:16.300
Did you all forget why you're here?

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:21.020
A reunion between long-wost sibwings?

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.070
A revenge pwot decades in the making?

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.540
A hero protecting his pwincess?

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.090
You certainly don't look 
very heroic right now.

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:33.180
What in the blue hell?

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:37.370
I went through all that twouble 
to tell y'all where Jinkoku-sha was

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.760
but you wouldn't do anything, 
so I went and ahead and captured them myself.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.150
See?

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:47.640
You...

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.150
Who the hell are you?

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:51.510
Who, me?

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.260
I'm Beta.

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:55.770
Beta...?

00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:58.990
I told you we'd meet again.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:02.580
Beta...

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:06.570
You're going down!

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.440
What are you going to do with Jinkoku-sha?

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:17.240
I could kill them, 
but that wouldn't be any fun.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:18.890
What the hell?!

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:23.500
Why don't you all come see me right now?

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:27.280
Remember the stadium built in this stage?

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:29.110
You'll find the thwee of them there.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:32.550
If you're intewested, 
get there on the double.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:35.560
To the stadium, now!

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:39.780
Doctor! Try to find 
where that message came from!

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.820
Already on it.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:44.350
But it's behind a billion proxies.

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:47.280
There's nothing useful 
in the police database,

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.860
and I can't access Iriya's from here!

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:54.380
Just who is Beta?

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:56.860
Keep going! It's that way!

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.180
<b>Tokyo Bay Megafloat - F Stage</b>

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:58.230
I know!

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:03.180
Okay, we've reached the stadium.

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:05.540
It's huge.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:08.520
You two are okay, eh?

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:10.330
Kondo!

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.780
Are you okay? You look hurt!

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:16.490
Yeah. She saved me 
when it was squeaky bum time.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.960
My dear!

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:21.660
Wait, Yggdrasil?

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:23.400
Indeed, it is I!

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.080
How are you in the real world?

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:27.080
What's going on?

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:33.700
I had Mama Kaori make me a body 
so I could help you.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.210
Also...

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:40.300
Something needs to be done about Alma. 
I'll get her back on our side.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.230
This way, Master.

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:47.260
Alma... Soma.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:54.280
Ah, I see we're all here.

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:58.030
Damn it, Nguyen! Open your eyes!

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:00.950
Awesome! The gang's all here!

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:04.520
Yoo-hoo! I'm over here!

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.290
So that's Beta!

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:12.540
No, that's a Bälz Inc. construction android. 
It must be remote-controlled.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:15.760
Indeed. This is my avatar out in society.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:17.610
I'm a very shy boy, you see.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:20.300
Anyway, here's what y'all came for!

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:23.140
Guys...

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:27.560
We came here like you asked! 
Now release them!

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:31.600
But I never said I'd fwee them if you came.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.900
By the way, do y'all hear that?

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:38.300
Finally, it's happening!

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:41.930
What is that? 
Switch to visuals outside the stadium.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:46.860
No way...

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:45.590
It stopped?

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:49.910
Look!

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:59.830
I knew you would come! But I was kinda afwaid 
you wouldn't for a while there.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:05.440
I'm the one running this auction. 
Not you, Beta.

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:08.120
Auctioneer.

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:09.270
That's him?

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:14.390
It took ten years, but I finally got you!

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.060
Ah, so it <i>was</i> you.

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:21.710
Hang on. You know who he is?

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:26.490
Tell me who Beta is, then!

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:31.700
I'm pretty sure you've met
him yourself, Natsume Akira.

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:37.660
On that day, ten years ago, 
Beta here did it.

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:45.280
He was the one who used EX-ARM
Number 11 to cause the Tokyo Attack!

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:54.760
So wait, that was Beta?!

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:57.040
What? You mean...

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:03.690
If what Auctioneer's saying is true, 
then Akira had nothing to do with it.

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:07.080
I need to apologize to you, Akira.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:08.650
It's fine, Minami.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:11.860
Even I'd forgotten I was innocent.

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:17.550
But you guys trusted me 
and let me fight alongside you,

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:20.380
and that helped me realize it wasn't me.

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:23.880
And now,

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:26.470
it's clear as day.

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:31.930
You are our biggest enemy!

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:37.640
I'm so happy you remember me now. 
Glad to see you haven't changed.

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:42.900
You had the same look 
in your eyes back then, too.

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:50.070
But what that also means is 
that I'm still better than you.

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:51.950
Now, then.

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:59.210
With the final bidders all here, 
I would like to begin the EX-ARM auction.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:04.710
That's what I like to hear. 
How much do you want for them?

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:06.920
I don't care about money.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.630
What I want is right there.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.060
It's Beta's head.

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:15.990
Whoever captures him gets all my EX-ARMs.

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:21.640
Are you sure? I might just kill these people 
if you twy to act all bossy with me.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:25.060
Don't you dare, Beta! 
Jinkoku-sha are ours to kill!

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:30.480
Okay, but then you know 
what you have to do, right?

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:34.670
Very well. We're taking
Auctioneer down, Alma.

00:08:34.670 --> 00:08:36.230
Understood, Master.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:41.770
I'm afraid I can't let that happen.

00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:44.410
I need those EX-ARMs.

00:08:45.030 --> 00:08:47.670
I won't be holding anything back.

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:50.590
Awesome! Now we're having some fun!

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:53.840
Hey! Don't forget you're dealing with me!

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:55.820
Wuv that energy.

00:08:55.820 --> 00:09:00.640
But you do weawize I hold Jinkoku-sha's lives 
in the palm of my hand, wight?

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:05.990
I will never take orders from you.

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:08.170
Grandfather...

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:15.320
I won't let the one who caused Japan's downfall 
from glory have his way again.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:19.160
You have one second to stop being annoying, 
or I weally will kill you.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.240
Kill me if you must!

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:26.080
Take me hostage all you want, 
I shall not kneel to you!

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:28.230
Okay, as you wish.

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:36.840
No! Grandfather!

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:39.760
Go to hell, Beta! He was my target!

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:43.200
Oh, I'm so sowwy! But relax. 
I avoided his vitals.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:44.720
You!

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:48.680
How I wuv those looks of despair 
on your faces.

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:52.640
Now, will this old man's fwiends 
rush to his aid?

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:57.180
What do you mean 
that you won't send help?!

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:01.680
Hayama Gaho is no longer indispensable 
to the Restoration Bloc.

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:03.560
And neither is the Counter EX-ARM Squad.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:06.490
Wait! They're trying to do their jobs!

00:10:06.490 --> 00:10:08.080
It's too late.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:13.800
We already asked Ichigaya 
to deploy the 13th Special Armored Squad.

00:10:14.690 --> 00:10:16.960
The 13th...?

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:18.220
It can't be!

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:21.770
Have a look. Aren't they awe-inspiring?

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:25.400
What are you going to do, Shiga?

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:30.280
<i>Don't worry. I expected the Bloc to do this.</i>

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:32.310
<i>That's why I'm here in the U.S. right now.</i>

00:10:32.740 --> 00:10:35.120
<i>I need you to deploy the thing 
we talked about.</i>

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:39.640
<i>I have an idea.</i>

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:43.740
Okay, we gotta take Auctioneer out.

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:47.580
The old man needs help. 
If we don't hurry, he's gonna croak.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:49.150
That's a bad idea.

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:53.130
There's no guarantee Beta will hold
up his end of the deal if we do as he says.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:56.510
I know that, man! 
But those two are in danger!

00:10:56.510 --> 00:11:01.080
Ygg and I will trap Beta online 
before he has the chance to do anything.

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:05.970
He's gotta be on the Megafloat's
network somewhere.

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:10.490
With Ygg's help, I can look
for him without being spotted.

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:13.800
If we can hold him off, 
we can rescue Jinkoku-sha!

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:16.380
Makes sense.

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:17.870
But how will you?

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:21.320
I've got a plan. Hear me out here.

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:24.640
Why would you side with Beta?

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:26.680
That isn't a very wise business move.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:29.130
I guess cops will be cops!

00:12:29.130 --> 00:12:31.530
Putting lives first, are we?

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:33.520
But you took too wong to choose.

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:35.940
How typical of the Japanese powice.

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:40.320
Not on my watch!

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:44.760
Okay, just as planned.

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:46.730
Back me up, Ygg!

00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:48.700
Yes, my dear!

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:03.020
Is this the realm representing 
the Megafloat's network?

00:13:03.020 --> 00:13:05.660
What's that huge wall, though?

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:09.440
It must be Beta's firewall!

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:12.060
So he's on the other side of this thing.

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:16.940
Indeed. But be careful, 
or he'll notice what we're doing.

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:19.980
And if he does, he might kill the hostages.

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:22.710
Let me build an attack code.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:29.400
I call it the Buster Sword. 
Use it to wreak havoc in this realm!

00:13:30.310 --> 00:13:33.760
He's been toying with me all this time.

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:35.870
It's finally my turn to counter.

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:40.040
Let's go!

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:41.000
Right!

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:43.000
<b>Illustration by Komi Shinya</b>

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:55.500
C'mon, cops, Jarde. 
You can do better than that.

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:59.270
Hurry up, or I might wose patience 
and kill them all.

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:01.270
God damn.

00:14:01.830 --> 00:14:03.770
He pisses me right off!

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:19.660
Midori?!

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:23.430
Yoo-hoo! I've been expecting you!

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:28.580
Beta...

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:33.340
You bitch!

00:14:33.340 --> 00:14:34.720
Oh, no, you don't.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:37.030
I can predict all your moves.

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:40.030
What? Is that all you've got?

00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:45.500
Remember, this is cyberspace. 
A program can take many forms in here.

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:49.320
Meaning I can even do this!

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:53.930
I've got you now!

00:14:54.450 --> 00:14:57.040
That's a neat little idea.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:15:00.970
But anything you can do,

00:15:00.970 --> 00:15:03.060
I can do better!

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:08.830
You and I are the same. Always have been.

00:15:08.830 --> 00:15:12.730
Shit... Who the hell <i>are</i> you?!

00:15:12.730 --> 00:15:16.890
Did you really forget? 
Search deep within your heart.

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:29.800
Number 00... Beta?!

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:37.080
Exactly. I'm another 
EX-ARM Number 00 like you.

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:42.300
My appearance is a straight copy of yours.

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:46.670
But you fought me in something else 
during the Tokyo Attack.

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:48.060
What was it, Ogre?

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:55.110
The combat android exoframe equipped with
the EX-ARM of the spinal cord, Number 01.

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:58.040
I know you used it after you reawakened, too.

00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:01.200
Its design has changed a lot 
since it got confiscated,

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:03.930
but the mainframe remains the same.

00:16:03.930 --> 00:16:07.230
Oh, so that's why I knew how to control it.

00:16:07.780 --> 00:16:12.720
I should've destroyed that thing 
together with Tokyo.

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:16.100
Wait, did you attack Tokyo 
to take Ogre out of the equation?

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:17.710
Of course not!

00:16:17.710 --> 00:16:19.320
Then why?

00:16:20.590 --> 00:16:22.280
"Why," you ask?

00:16:23.110 --> 00:16:26.150
All I did was do 
what humans have always done.

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:30.600
Think back through history.

00:16:30.600 --> 00:16:34.940
Endless killing, looting, and destruction.

00:16:34.940 --> 00:16:37.450
And I copied that.

00:16:38.130 --> 00:16:39.510
Just kidding!

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:46.580
What'd you think? 
Sounded like a convincing reason, right?

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:52.120
C'mon, man! Who needs a reason to
squash them like the little bugs they are?!

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:55.740
But I guess if I had to say, 
it was because it seemed fun!

00:16:57.520 --> 00:17:00.040
After that little push I gave them that day,

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:03.830
the humans dove headfirst 
into an endless cycle of tragedy.

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:07.540
One of poverty, plundering, and revenge...

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:10.000
One where malice bred further malice!

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.380
Could you ask for a more entertaining show?!

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:15.800
You're insane.

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:18.860
Huh? What's with the scary look?

00:17:18.860 --> 00:17:22.220
I'm sure you see where I'm coming from.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:28.580
Your happiness lies in constant battle.

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:33.570
I told you we're the same.

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:43.370
I know you had fun 
letting the hatred consume you!

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:49.340
Sure, I was one step away 
from ending up like you.

00:17:49.340 --> 00:17:50.950
But I...

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:55.590
I haven't lost faith like you have!

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:00.880
What are you playing at? It's too late.

00:18:00.880 --> 00:18:04.230
Don't think things will keep going your way!

00:18:04.710 --> 00:18:05.770
Now, Ygg!

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:07.690
Yes, my dear!

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:08.950
What?!

00:18:10.420 --> 00:18:13.190
Break through the cage's program!

00:18:18.640 --> 00:18:20.950
The cage is open, my dear!

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:22.410
Damn it!

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:25.960
Nice! Log out!

00:18:27.890 --> 00:18:28.730
Got it!

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:32.130
Tch.

00:18:34.790 --> 00:18:36.730
We can escape, Grandfather.

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:41.540
Ygg! Keep them safe!

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:43.540
You got it!

00:18:45.840 --> 00:18:48.060
You're not going anywhere.

00:18:48.770 --> 00:18:50.010
Midori!

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:52.600
Midori!

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:56.690
Miyabe?

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:58.200
Out of my way.

00:19:01.940 --> 00:19:03.350
Miyabe!

00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:11.500
Hurry up and run! Miyabe died for you!

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:15.770
This way!

00:19:15.770 --> 00:19:16.680
Yes!

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:26.680
After them!

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:31.670
Not so fast.

00:19:35.220 --> 00:19:38.690
<i>"Not so fast"? 
You took the words out of my mouth!</i>

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:48.370
Damn, is Beta controlling 
all these construction androids?

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:49.260
Minami!

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:57.590
<i>Your hands are tied out there. 
Not that you have hands wight now!</i>

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:02.560
Man, we wouldn't be in this situation 
if I could use Ogre!

00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:04.890
Something seems off, my dear.

00:20:05.210 --> 00:20:07.500
Miyabe's corpse is gone.

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:08.660
What?!

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:11.560
<i>Aw.</i>

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:14.070
<i>That sucks.</i>

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:16.700
<i>I guess you realized.</i>

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:21.860
No... You were Beta all along, Miyabe?!

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:24.280
<i>Bingo!</i>

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:33.350
<i>I took over his body 
before the whole auction began.</i>

00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:35.660
What?!

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:40.730
Wait... With his body, 
he could keep tabs on our squad

00:20:40.730 --> 00:20:43.420
<i>and</i> manipulate them!

00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:49.850
And it gave him the perfect chance 
to bring Jinkoku-sha here from the hideout!

00:20:50.200 --> 00:20:51.480
<i>Surprised?</i>

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:55.840
<i>It's a shame. He was pretty useful.</i>

00:20:55.840 --> 00:21:00.650
The entire time you watched us, 
you were laughing at us inside, weren't you?!

00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:02.970
<i>Well, let's resume, shall we?</i>

00:21:04.680 --> 00:21:06.580
<i>Oh, what's this?</i>

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:11.140
Are you kidding me? This is really bad news!

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:13.410
Get down, Minami!

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:22.300
Bombers?

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:24.640
No, that's not it.

00:21:24.640 --> 00:21:26.340
The hell are those things?

00:21:26.900 --> 00:21:31.430
The JDF's multibots, code-named Amaterasu!

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:33.690
Amaterasu...

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:39.560
<i>This party's really getting started now.</i>

00:21:40.260 --> 00:21:43.770
<i>What will you do now, Natsume Akira?</i>

00:21:48.480 --> 00:21:50.070
Beta!

00:23:25.910 --> 00:23:29.420
I've never forgotten this rage 
burning within me.

00:23:29.820 --> 00:23:33.010
My only purpose in life has been 
to settle my score with him.

00:23:33.400 --> 00:23:37.220
Next time, on <i>EX-ARM:</i> 
"Battle 009 - Fallen Messiah."

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Fallen Messiah</b>

00:23:37.220 --> 00:23:39.540
I'll put an end to this myself!
